From 0ca1aad68b9ac13b50e9aa1ca462d78aadf9ac56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:53:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 114/115] hir_typeck: `Self` in a trait's provided methods is
 ?Sized unless bounded

cipher 0.5.1 (rars 0.9.4) stream.rs:159, a provided method of StreamCipher:

    fn try_write_keystream(&mut self, buf: &mut [u8]) -> Result<(), StreamCipherError> {
        self.check_remaining(buf.len())?;   // fn check_remaining(&self, ..)
    impl<C: StreamCipher> StreamCipher for &mut C { .. }

Method lookup tried `<&mut Self as StreamCipher>::check_remaining` (autoref
of the `&mut Self` receiver) and accepted the blanket impl, because
TraitResolution::type_is_sized assumed sized for any generic it didn't
know, including `Self`. The impl's `C` is implicitly Sized and a trait's
`Self` isn't, so rustc rejects that candidate and takes
`<Self as StreamCipher>` at the next autoderef step. The post-typeck
check (StaticTraitResolve, which gets this right) then failed: "Cannot
find an impl of ::cipher::stream::StreamCipher for &mut Self".

type_is_sized now answers Unequal for `Self` after the bound search above
it found no `Sized` bound (`trait X: Sized`, a supertrait such as Clone,
or `where Self: Sized`). `Self` only survives into typeck in trait bodies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
index d5ba7c5d..5bc71028 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/helpers.cpp
@@ -4236,6 +4236,12 @@ bool TraitResolution::trait_contains_type(const Span& sp, const ::HIR::GenericPa
         )
         }
     TU_ARMA(Generic, e) {
+        // `Self` (only left in trait bodies) is `?Sized` unless bounded, and the bounds were searched above. As in
+        // StaticTraitResolve, so that a blanket `impl<C: Tr> Tr for &mut C` isn't picked for `&mut Self`.
+        // - cipher 0.5.1: `self.check_remaining(..)` in `StreamCipher::try_write_keystream`
+        if( e.binding == GENERIC_Self ) {
+            return ::HIR::Compare::Unequal;
+        }
 
         switch(e.group())
         {
